{
  "contract": "se1 secret envelope (exponetdb/secret/v1, exponetdb/data-key/v1)",
  "specification": "exponetdb-docs/08-auth-and-security/secrets.md#21-envelope-format-se1",
  "notes": "Keys, data keys and nonces are synthetic test values (SHA-256 chains of labels), never real material. random gives the bytes an implementation draws, in order: data key (32), wrap nonce (12), nonce (12). wrappedKeyHex is AES-256-GCM(masterKey, wrapNonce, dataKey, AAD = dataKeyAad) as ciphertext followed by the 16-byte tag; ciphertextHex is AES-256-GCM(dataKey, nonce, plaintext, AAD = aad), same layout. checkValue is hmac-sha256: plus hex HMAC-SHA-256(masterKey, \"exponetdb/master-key-check/v1\"). expectedError is the first failing check of the context, in the order secret id, purpose, subject, version, key id.",
